# 9. ASYNCHRONOUS BATCH PROCESSING

Use Celery with Redis.

Implement a task such as:

process_inspection(inspection_id)

The task should:

1. Load the inspection record.
2. Confirm the item is eligible for processing.
3. Set its status to PROCESSING.
4. Load the stored image.
5. Call the shared AI model service.
6. Save the real prediction.
7. Save supported confidence information.
8. Record the model version.
9. Mark the inspection COMPLETED.
10. Record completion time.
11. Handle exceptions.
12. Mark failed items as FAILED with a readable error.
13. Update batch progress.
14. Update the overall batch status.

Use transactions and locking where needed to prevent conflicting updates.

Avoid scheduling the same item more than once.

Do not block the HTTP request while all images are being processed.

The API should return the batch ID and the initial item statuses.

The frontend should poll a batch-status endpoint or use another suitable mechanism to refresh progress.

A batch should be marked:

* COMPLETED when all accepted items finish successfully.
* COMPLETED_WITH_ERRORS when some items fail or are rejected but processing otherwise finishes.
* FAILED when the batch cannot be processed as a whole.

Define the exact aggregation logic consistently.

Keep accepted, rejected, completed, and failed counts accurate.

